  "paper": "paper_1a",
  "question": {
    "html": "<p>The centre of the Earth and the Moon are a distance <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"D\"></span> apart. There is a point X between them where their gravitational fields cancel out. The distance from the centre of the Earth to X is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"d\"></span>. The mass of the Earth is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"M_{E}\"></span> and the mass of the Moon is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"M_{M}\"></span>.</p>\n<p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure></p>\n<p>What is correct at X?</p>\n<p>[1]</p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{M_{E}}{d}=\\frac{M_{M}}{D-d}\"></span></li><li data-label=\"B\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{M_{E}}{D-d}=\\frac{M_{M}}{d}\"></span></li><li data-label=\"C\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{M_{E}}{d^{2}}=\\frac{M_{M}}{D-d^{2}}\"></span></li><li data-label=\"D\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{M_{E}}{d^{2}}=\\frac{M_{M}}{D^{2}-d^{2}}\"></span></li></ol>"
  },
